Worktree: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/182-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (your current directory).
Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make one change in two sibling adapters, plus their tests.

Problem: `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs` and `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/devin/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs` decide whether to log a command with `DISPATCH_SHAPES.find((candidate) => candidate.test.test(command))`, a raw regex over the whole text. So a command that only writes a dispatch into heredoc data, such as `cat > run.sh <<'EOF'` / `opencode run -m p/m x` / `EOF`, is logged as a dispatch, while the Claude, OpenCode and Pi adapters, which call `recordDispatch` from `../lib/dispatch-audit.mjs`, resolve the command first and do not log it.

Fix, in each of the two files:
1. Replace the raw `DISPATCH_SHAPES.find(...)` match and the hand-built `extractDispatchMeta` / `buildAuditLine` / `appendAuditLog` sequence with one `recordDispatch({ command, logPath, runtime, sessionID, callID, outputText, metadataObj, env: process.env })` call, the way `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/claude/dispatch-audit-posttooluse.mjs` does. Keep each adapter's own `runtime` tag (`'codex'`, `'devin'`), its own tool-name check, its own project-directory and log-path logic, its own `outputText` and `metadataObj` derivation, and `sessionID: payload?.session_id ?? null`, `callID: payload?.tool_use_id ?? null`.
2. Remove the imports that become unused. Keep the import grouping the files already use.
3. Update each header comment so it no longer says the adapter matches the shape list itself.

Tests:
- In `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/codex/codex-shell-tool.test.mjs`, inside `describe('Codex dispatch audit', ...)`, add one `it` that runs the audit hook with `tool_name: 'Bash'`, a fresh temporary `cwd`, and `tool_input.command` set to `"cat > run.sh <<'EOF'\nopencode run -m p/m x\nEOF"`, then asserts exit status 0 and that `.skilled/logs/cli-dispatch-audit.log` under that `cwd` does NOT exist. Clean up the temporary directory in `finally`, as the existing test does.
- Create `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/devin/devin-dispatch-audit.test.mjs` (vitest, same header style and the same `hookEnv` / `runHook` helpers as the Codex test file) with two tests: a dispatch `opencode run -m p/m "x" </dev/null` sent with `tool_name: 'exec'` and a temporary `cwd` writes one log line whose `runtime` is `'devin'`; the heredoc-only command above writes no log.

Comments keep the durable WHY and never name spec paths, phases, or task, review or finding ids.

